  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING ANTI-POACHING OPERATIONS AND COMMUNITY ENGAGEMENT TO PROTECT ELEPHANTS IN A CRITICAL AREA OF NIASSA RESERVE, MOZAMBIQUE</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">STRENGTHENING ANTI-POACHING OPERATIONS AND COMMUNITY ENGAGEMENT TO PROTECT ELEPHANTS IN A CRITICAL AREA OF NIASSA RESERVE, MOZAMBIQUE. IN PARTNERSHIP WITH FAUNA FLORA INTERNATIONAL. THE PURPOSE OF THIS PROJECT IS TO SUPPORT AN ELEPHANT CONSERVATION EFFORT IN NIASSA RESERVE BY MAINTAINING AND STRENGTHENING ANTIPOACHING EFFORTS IN A SEVERELY DEPLETED ELEPHANT POPULATION IN NORTHERN MOZAMBIQUE. ESTIMATED TO CONTAIN OVER 12,000 ELEPHANTS IN 2011, THE NIASSA NATIONAL RESERVE (NOW THE NIASSA SPECIAL RESERVE) IS REPORTED TO HAVE LOST OVER 60 OF ITS ELEPHANTS BY 2014 DURING A POACHING SURGE DESCRIBED AS ONE OF THE MOST CATASTROPHIC DECLINES ON THE CONTINENT. ONE OF MULTIPLE CONCESSION GROUPINGS WITHIN NIASSA, THE CHUILEXI CONSERVANCY IS BELIEVED TO CONTAIN A DISPROPORTIONATE NUMBER OF THE REMAINING ELEPHANTS AND WILL BE AN IMPORTANT SOURCE POPULATION FOR THE RESERVE S RECOVERY IF A RECENT REDUCTION IN POACHING CAN BE MAINTAINED. SPECIFIC ACTIVITIES INCLUDE: (1) MAINTAINING ANTI-POACHING OPERATIONS, INCLUDING SUPPORT FOR PATROL TRANSPORT, EQUIPMENT, AND AERIAL MONITORING (2) IMPROVING MONITORING AND PROTECTION CAPACITY, INCLUDING AN UPGRADED OPERATIONS ROOMS FOR LAW ENFORCEMENT, AND TRAINING IN LAW ENFORCEMENT MONITORING AND DECISION-MAKING SOFTWARE SYSTEMS (3) CONDUCTING PUBLIC ENGAGEMENT AND OUTREACH WITH LOCAL CO</narrative>
  </description>
